  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` events now carry `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside the old `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The values are identical, and nothing was removed or renamed, so existing consumers are unaffected. All 39 tests pass, and `npm run arch` finds no dependency violations. I didn't run `npm run typecheck`.\n\n- **Change:** the interface and the `orderPlaced()` builder are in `src/core/events.ts`. I updated the event assertion in `test/app.test.ts` to expect the new fields.\n- **Schema version:** I left it at 3, since adding fields doesn't break consumers that ignore unknown ones. If any consumer validates strictly against the v3 schema, it would reject the extra fields. In that case, bump to 4 and announce it.\n- **HTTP response:** I didn't touch the `POST /orders` response (`totalCents`, `placedAt`). You asked about the event, and that response shape is documented in `CLAUDE.md` and the README. Say if you want it aligned too.\n- **Retiring the old names:** once consumers have moved to `amountCents` and `createdAt`, you can drop `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event. That removal would need a new schema version.\n\nI also mistyped a path partway through, and the harness denied that read. It had no effect, and I redid it with the right path.",
